# Trivy vulnerability-ignore list for the codingenv image
# (used via --ignorefile in .gitea/workflows/codingenv-rebuild.yml).
#
# npm bundled with node 24.20.0 pins transitive deps whose fixes are
# published upstream (brace-expansion >= 5.0.9, ip-address >= 10.3.1,
# tar >= 7.5.22), but they are unreachable right now: fresh npm installs
# are broken (@npmcli/docs was unpublished from the npm registry) and an
# in-place `npm install -g npm@...` keeps the old pinned versions.
#
# Re-check after every NODE_VERSION bump (codingenv/.env.sample): once a Node
# release bundles an npm with the fixed pins, remove the entries below.

CVE-2026-14257
CVE-2026-69152
CVE-2026-69192
CVE-2026-73566

# Added 2026-09-30, same situation: npm's bundled brace-expansion 5.0.7
# (fixed >= 5.0.10 / 5.0.11) and undici 6.27.0 (fixed >= 6.28.1). No npm
# release bundles the fixed versions yet -- not even npm 12.1.0 (latest,
# brace-expansion 5.0.9 / undici 6.28.0), nor the npm in Node 24.21.0 LTS /
# 26.10.0 (npm 11.19.x). Remove once a Node/npm release ships them.
CVE-2026-102276
CVE-2026-102278
CVE-2026-19534

# Three Go DoS CVEs (Added 2026-10-10 in the since-removed claude-env /
# opencode-env images, carried over 2026-10-23 when gh/glab/tea landed
# here): net/http Range-header handling (server-side; these are clients),
# crypto/tls ECH extension parsing, and HTTP/2 SETTINGS flooding
# (CVE-2026-78669, in both stdlib and x/net). Fixed in Go 1.27.2 / 1.26.9
# and x/net 0.60.0. Still reported (local scan, fresh DB, 2026-10-23) for:
#   - tea 0.16.0 (Gitea CLI; Go 1.26.6 + x/net 0.57.0, no newer release)
#   - yq 4.54.1 (x/net 0.59.0 -- only CVE-2026-78669)
# gh is clean again since 2.103.0 (Go 1.27.3); glab 1.124.0 is clean for
# these three. Only drop an id once no binary is reported for it.
CVE-2026-78667
CVE-2026-97031
CVE-2026-78669

# Added 2026-10-23: Go crypto/x509 denylist for distrusted intermediate
# certificates (published 2026-10-21, fixed in Go 1.27.3 / 1.26.10). It
# guards platforms whose trust store isn't updated; on Linux Go uses the
# system roots, and this image's apt layer refreshes ca-certificates on every
# daily rebuild, so the practical exposure is low. Reported for glab 1.124.0
# (Go 1.27.2), tea 0.16.0 (Go 1.26.6) and yq 4.54.1 (Go 1.27.1); none has a
# release built with a fixed Go yet. Remove once all three have one (CI
# bumps glab/tea/yq on its own).
CVE-2026-111943
